{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01B314wF1UyHbh7m7dnYkdPN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor â€” Productivity System for J.C. Liechty**\n\n- **What it is:** A single-folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), stdlib-only Python productivity system whose source of truth is plain markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files, etc.) â€” no database, no external dependencies (one declared exception: optional `pywinpty` for terminals).\n\n- **Core app it ships:** `anchor_gui.py` â€” a self-contained local web server bound to `http://localhost:8777`, run persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`. It generates the full dashboard HTML on every request and reads/writes the markdown directly. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) provides the same task logic plus static `dashboard.html` generation.\n\n- **Primary purpose (task management):** Capture and move tasks through a lifecycle â€” Active â†’ Done/Cancelled/Saved-for-Later/Restored â€” across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing). Fully interactive in the browser (check off, add, capture, edit), with every change logged to daily logs.\n\n- **What grew on top (R&D control surface):** A multi-version subsystem (v2 â†’ v3 â†’ v4 \"Project Cockpit\", all built/merged to master) that turns each project into a mission-control window for \"trio\" work â€” the **researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman** skill pipeline (Research Â· Planning Â· Build lanes).\n\n- **What the cockpit does:** Renders each lane as a tile with one honest status light (green/amber/red/grey), expands an **inline panel in place** (summary on top, real resizable xterm.js terminal below), runs real server-side **ConPTY terminal sessions** isolated per-session via git worktrees, loads each lane's skill **once** (greet-once, no repeating-prompt loop), supports a claudeâ†”gemini engine toggle, cached/validated session+project summaries, cost/tokens/time rollups, a grass-catcher idea board, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **Reliability scaffolding it ships:** A daily 5 AM health-check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) that parses every markdown file and walks the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (never the live service or real `claude`), writing dated reports and surfacing a red dashboard banner on failure.\n\n- **Branding/framing:** Presented as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢,\" with a vendored brand mark used as favicon and masthead lockup.\n\nThese are grounded in the project's `CLAUDE.md` and the locked North-Star/design docs; the v4 status is recorded as built (9 waves GREEN, 637 passed) and merged to master as of 2026-06-13."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45810,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6def9e2b-d45a-4352-bcbe-2a6f73b2a0bf","uuid":"8ba6a383-59d1-416a-b7a6-44c2298d2ed0","request_id":"req_011Cc2Me8iB1MWpDPdwzZz1w"}
